This is a placeholder. A real DOS 3.3 disk image needs to be created with disk authoring tools.

To create a bootable WIKI.DSK file:

1. Use CiderPress (Windows/Mac) or Apple II Disk Utility to create a new DOS 3.3 disk image
2. Copy these files to the disk:
   - WIKI.BASIC (as BASIC program)
   - ARTICLES.DATA (as binary data file)
   - README (as text file)

Alternatively, use tools like:
- AppleWin (Windows emulator with disk tools)
- MESS/MAME (cross-platform emulator)
- Disc Copy (original Apple utility)

The disk image format should be:
- Format: 140KB 5.25" floppy (standard DOS 3.3)
- Filename: WIKI.DSK
- Bootable: Yes (with DOS 3.3 system files)
